// Quiz for Iterators
::Iterators::
What is an iterator in Python?{
~A data structure used to store a collection of items
~A function that calls itself within its definition
=An object that allows traversal through elements of a collection
~A built-in Python module for handling file input/output
}

::Iterators::
Which of the following statements about iterators in Python is true?{
~Iterators can only move forward through a collection of elements
~Iterators are limited to operating on numeric data types
=The iter() function is used to create an iterator from an iterable object
~Iterators can access elements in a collection randomly without following a sequence
}

::Iterators::
How do you retrieve the next element from an iterator in Python?{
~Using the prev() method
~Using the get_next() method
=Using the next() function
~Using the retrieve() method
}
